  "findings": [
    "BytesToKilobytesConverter divides long bytes by 1024 before casting to decimal, truncating fractional kilobytes. ConvertBack rounds decimal to Int64 before multiplying; size-filter UI impact requires binding review.",
    "AllTrueToTrueConverter returns true for an empty list, while OneTrueToTrueConverter returns false; this follows All/Any semantics, and no defect is asserted without caller context. IntToTrueConverter directly casts value and parameter to int.",
    "Display converters handle booleans, nulls, wrapping, strike-through and theme brush selection. Most ConvertBack methods throw NotImplementedException; actual binding modes remain to inspect.",
    "Default marking criterion is newest modified; default excluded extensions include executables, shared libraries and scripts. MarkingCriteria enum describes keeping a representative; actual grouping/locking/tie behavior remains unread.",
    "Directory.Build.props defines AvaloniaVersion 11.1.0 while main project references explicit 12.0.x packages; whether the shared property affects other projects remains unqualified.",
    "linux_build.sh does not stop on build failure, overwrites run.sh with a hardcoded Debug/net8.0-windows path, then launches it in background. This script was read only, not executed."
